{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789780620,"nonce":"Lue/eEJcsBplnBXi5WADJiCHZnE=","title":"Loop OSR stubs hand the frame to the body through per-function words shared by all threads","message":"The rt seam test (`the_threads_that_run_wren_and_their_waits_reach_the_seam`) aborted now and then on the LLVM legs of CI: SIGABRT on ubuntu, 0xc0000374 on Windows. Under a debugger the abort is a realloc of a freed buffer in `ObjList::ensure_capacity`, reached from `wren_list_add` inside an OSR'd baseline loop.\n\nReproducer: four `Thread.create` bodies that each build their own list in a 5000-iteration loop (`xs.add([k])`). Plain `wlift` hits it about once in 1600 runs; with the compile-time safepoint poll off it is about 7 in 1600. Clean under GC stress, with the interpreter only, with `WLIFT_TIER1=off`, or with `WLIFT_DISABLE_METHOD_OSR=1`.\n\nWhat was refuted: the allocator never hands out an address twice; the post-collection fiber verifier never fires; each list is created once. A collision detector in `wren_list_add` showed two OS threads inside `add` on one list, and the intruder's interpreter frame never held that list: its compiled loop was running with another task's `xs` as a live-in.\n\nCause: `define_osr_stubs` wrote `(entry index, frame pointer)` into a static per-function pair of words and the body's entry read them back. Two threads entering the same loop at once could each read the other's frame. A first attempt passed the frame tagged in the body's first argument, which fixed nothing here because the closure has arity 0 and no argument to carry it.\n\nFix: the stub calls `wren_osr_post`, which keeps the frame in the thread's JIT state and raises the body's pending count; the body's entry checks the count and, when set, calls `wren_osr_take` for its own thread's frame, falling through to the normal entry when another thread raised it. The entry index sits in the word before the live-ins, which `try_enter_loop_osr` and `wren_retier` reserve.\n\nAfter the fix: 2400 runs of the reproducer with the poll off and 1600 runs of the seam test on each of the Cranelift and LLVM builds, all clean.","files":null}]}